---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import CrossSell from '../../components/CrossSell.astro';
---
<Base title="Requesting a skill — Recipes Docs">
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 pt-16 pb-12">
    <p class="eyebrow mb-2">Documentation · Skill requests</p>
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight mb-6">Don't publish. Request.</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Recipes is a <strong>single-publisher catalog</strong>. Every skill is curated and
        maintained by the WiseChef team. We don't take submissions — we take requests.
      </p>

      <p>
        Tell us what's broken in your fleet, what your team is doing manually that should
        be automated, or what your agent fails at and we'll ship a skill that fixes it.
      </p>

      <h2>Why single-publisher?</h2>
      <p>
        Building a publisher trust ladder before publishers exist is wasted work. We want
        the catalog to be excellent, not large. Every skill on Recipes was authored against
        a real production failure mode. That's the bar.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Fewer skills, deeper coverage.</li>
        <li>One quality bar — ours.</li>
        <li>Auto-improve telemetry feeds back into the next version.</li>
        <li>Architecture-aware install means the skill won't crash on your hardware.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How to request a skill</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Go to <a href="https://recipes.wisechef.ai/request-skill">/request-skill</a> and submit the form (or DM <a href="https://wisechef.ai">WiseChef</a> directly).</li>
        <li>We triage requests by signal: how many fleets would use this, how broken is the alternative, how recurring is the pain.</li>
        <li>Time-to-skill for matched requests: 7 days for a working install, 14 days for full polish.</li>
        <li>Operator subscribers get priority + a dedicated review SLA.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>What makes a good request</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>A real workflow your team runs (or wants to run) repeatedly.</li>
        <li>The hours/week that go into it manually today.</li>
        <li>The failure mode you'd want telemetry on.</li>
        <li>Whether the result needs a UI, a report, an API call, or just a side-effect.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>The future of publishing</h2>
      <p>
        We may open invitation-only publishing later, with explicit per-publisher
        agreements and 1:1 onboarding. We will <em>never</em> automate it. If you think
        you're an exception, <a href="https://recipes.wisechef.ai/request-skill">tell us</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
    <CrossSell />
  </section>
</Base>
